{title: My Lord and My God}
{subtitle: John 20:24–29}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
They [Bb]came to me with open hands and [Eb]said we've seen the Lord
I [Gm]shook my head and turned away, I [Eb]would not take their word
Un[Gm]less I see the mark of nails and [Eb]touch them with my hand
Un[Cm7]less I touch his wounded side, I [Eb]cannot understand [Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Eight days later we were gathered and the [Eb]doors were locked again
He [Gm]came and stood among us and he [Eb]spoke to all of them
[Gm]Peace be with you, said the Master, and he [Eb]turned his eyes to me
He [Cm7]did not scold, he did not shame, he [Eb]showed his hands to me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Cm7]Put your finger [Eb]here
Look at my [Bb]hands
[Cm7]Reach out your hand [Cm/D]and put [Eb]it into my side
Stop [F]doubting and believe
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My [Bb]Lord and my [Eb]God
My [Gm]Lord and my [Eb]God
[Bb]Blessed are those who have not [Eb]seen and yet have be[Bb]lieved
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
We [Gm]never saw the empty tomb, we [Eb]never touched his hand
But the [Gm]word has come to us ac[Eb]ross the sea and land
So [Gm]we are in the blessing that he spoke [Eb]inside that room
For [Cm7]those who have not seen him ri[Eb]sen from the [Bb]tomb
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My Lord and my [Eb]God
My [Gm7]Lord and my [Eb]God
[Bb]Blessed are those who have not [Eb]seen and yet have be[Bb]lieved
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
My Lord and my [Eb]God
{end_of_verse}
